Modifications made by the CatTunnel authors include, but are not limited to:

- Rebranding: app name, package identifier, icons, splash screen and
  in-app text; Russian localization and a language switch; onboarding.
- Servers: kill switch, auto-connect and auto-reconnect, tt:// server link
  export/import with QR codes, MTU configuration, server latency testing and
  sorting, a consolidated "Add Server" flow.
- Subscriptions: server subscriptions with per-subscription sync,
  age-encrypted subscription responses (binary and ASCII armor), grouping by
  subscription, sharing and importing a subscription via QR.
- Connection: Quick Settings tile, a single connection notification,
  stuck-connection diagnostics ("Marsik": internet, TCP, TLS/SNI,
  credentials and subscription checks).
- Security: strict server certificate verification that excludes
  user-installed and "Russian Trusted" CAs, phone security check, leak check,
  panic button (wipe app data), launcher disguise, app lock, FLAG_SECURE on
  screens that show keys.
- Privacy hardening: log sanitizer for subscription URLs and age keys,
  https-only subscriptions without redirects, no cloud/device-transfer
  backups, connection query log kept only per session, ML Kit usage
  reporting disabled.
- A cat companion (petting, compliments, purr sound).
- Licenses of the native VPN engine's and Android dependencies added to the
  in-app license page (assets/licenses/).
- In-app updates on Android (latest.json from a download server given at
  build time, sha256-checked APK handed to the system installer).
- One engine version for all platforms (ENGINE_VERSION,
  tools/update_engine.sh); Windows build branding.
- Anti-DPI: an own build of the native engine (tools/engine_native) that
  sends the TLS ClientHello with ByeDPI-style techniques, including a custom
  split string; a ClientHello fingerprint per server.
- Appearance: a dark theme derived from the original palette, and a
  «Cozy» style with a big connect button, session timer and server picker.

